1
00:00:00,390 --> 00:00:04,720
You have a heart, a liver, a pair of lungs. Rank them.
Decide which one matters most,

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:09,610
and which one you could most easily do without, and notice
how quickly you started sorting them.

3
00:00:11,025 --> 00:00:14,170
Two thousand years ago an emperor asked a physician that
exact question,

4
00:00:14,170 --> 00:00:18,975
and got back an answer that has outlived every anatomy it
was built on. He was told his body was a government.

5
00:00:20,505 --> 00:00:23,378
I want a ranking. Every court has one, every ministry has
one,

6
00:00:23,378 --> 00:00:27,734
and a physician who tells me all my organs are equally
precious has never had to cut a budget.

7
00:00:27,734 --> 00:00:29,495
Which of them is noble? Which is base?

8
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:34,183
That is a most thorough question, and I am going to answer
a slightly different one,

9
00:00:34,183 --> 00:00:38,484
because the ranking you are asking for does not exist at
all. What exists instead is an arrangement,

10
00:00:38,484 --> 00:00:39,430
and I will set it out.

11
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:44,493
He asked for a hierarchy and was handed an organisation
chart. Twelve organs,

12
00:00:44,493 --> 00:00:49,060
each given an office of state with a job title and a product.
Nobody had described a body that way.

13
00:00:50,515 --> 00:00:55,780
The book is the Basic Questions, the first half of the Yellow
Emperor's Inner Canon. Its title names a room:

14
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:59,485
the Chamber of the Numinous Orchid, where the Emperor
locked this text away.

15
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:05,719
This is The Emperor's Inner Canon, and this episode is
called The Twelve Offices. One metaphor, twelve jobs,

16
00:01:05,719 --> 00:01:09,460
and an argument about what a good metaphor costs you
once it stops letting go.

17
00:01:10,465 --> 00:01:13,388
Before anybody starts, I am writing all of this down. Twelve
organs and twelve offices,

18
00:01:13,388 --> 00:01:15,000
and I intend to check the arithmetic at the end,

19
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,561
because in my experience a government always turns out to
have one more department than anybody admits to.

20
00:01:18,561 --> 00:01:19,535
Nobody ever thanks me for it.

21
00:01:20,635 --> 00:01:24,977
Watch it do real work first. This is not decoration, it is a
model, and it makes predictions.

22
00:01:24,977 --> 00:01:29,365
Then watch the same metaphor become the reason nobody
could correct it for two thousand years.

23
00:01:30,905 --> 00:01:34,375
The heart is the office of the sovereign ruler. From it issue
spirit and illumination.

24
00:01:34,375 --> 00:01:39,095
Everything else in this list is arranged around that one
sentence, so I would rather you did not let it pass quickly.

25
00:01:40,790 --> 00:01:45,111
Sovereign is a precise word here. Not the largest organ, not
the strongest, not even the busiest.

26
00:01:45,111 --> 00:01:49,210
The one the others answer to, and the one whose failure is
a failure of everything below it.

27
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:54,558
And spirit and illumination is one term, shen ming. It covers
consciousness, clarity, judgment,

28
00:01:54,558 --> 00:01:59,640
the thing that knows it is thinking. The chapter puts all of
that inside the chest, deliberately, and never wavers.

29
00:02:00,915 --> 00:02:04,720
Then my heart is me. Not a pump or a muscle or a piece of
offal that a butcher would recognise,

30
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:09,085
but the very seat of the sovereign, which is remarkably
convenient for me, because I happen to be one myself.

31
00:02:10,990 --> 00:02:14,065
The heart is the office. You are not the office, and neither is
the organ.

32
00:02:14,065 --> 00:02:19,010
That distinction is the whole method of this chapter, and it
is why the list survived every anatomy that came after it.

33
00:02:20,555 --> 00:02:25,230
We should say the plain thing now rather than leaving it to
the end. Consciousness is not produced in the heart.

34
00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:29,445
It is produced in the brain, and on this particular point the
chapter is simply and completely wrong.

35
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:36,231
What makes that interesting is that the same canon knows
about the brain, calling it elsewhere the sea of marrow,

36
00:02:36,231 --> 00:02:38,920
so the organ is described and simply never given an office.

37
00:02:40,990 --> 00:02:45,455
So this is not ignorance. It is a decision about who
governs, taken early, written into the vocabulary,

38
00:02:45,455 --> 00:02:49,010
and then defended by every sentence built on top of it for
the next two millennia.

39
00:02:50,665 --> 00:02:53,567
Then I have my first finding already, and we are only one
office into this list.

40
00:02:53,567 --> 00:02:56,179
There is no seat on this council for the organ that is doing
the asking.

41
00:02:56,179 --> 00:02:59,335
The brain is not junior here and it is not waiting outside.
The brain is simply absent.

42
00:03:00,290 --> 00:03:05,126
He is right, and the wording matters. The brain was not
demoted, because it was never nominated.

43
00:03:05,126 --> 00:03:09,710
Nothing here argues the heart won. There is only an
assumption it never once had to defend.

44
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:15,497
Second office, and it is also the second seat. The lung is
the chancellor, the minister who stands beside the throne.

45
00:03:15,497 --> 00:03:19,560
From it issue regulation and rhythm, and no other organ is
placed that close to the sovereign.

46
00:03:20,330 --> 00:03:24,037
Chancellor undersells it. The term is closer to minister and
mentor together,

47
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:29,670
the official who advises the ruler and administers what the
ruler decides. Second in the state and first in practice.

48
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:36,914
Regulation and rhythm is also one term, zhi jie. Jie is the
joint in a bamboo, the notch and the measured interval.

49
00:03:36,914 --> 00:03:39,200
The lung keeps everything else on the beat.

50
00:03:40,730 --> 00:03:44,938
You can hear the argument for it quite easily. Breath is the
one process a person can actually watch,

51
00:03:44,938 --> 00:03:49,270
and it never stops, and everything else keeps its time
against it. You would seat him beside the throne.

52
00:03:50,915 --> 00:03:55,900
And this one scores. Your lungs really are a regulator. They
set the acidity of your blood minute by minute,

53
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:59,085
by deciding how much carbon dioxide to keep and how
much to blow off.

54
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:05,572
The rhythm claim lands too. Your heart rate rises as you
breathe in and it falls again as you breathe out,

55
00:04:05,572 --> 00:04:09,700
all day long without pause. The lung is setting a beat that
the heart then follows.

56
00:04:10,770 --> 00:04:13,416
Mark that carefully, because the pattern repeats all
episode.

57
00:04:13,416 --> 00:04:16,106
The chapter is right about the job and wrong about the
reason,

58
00:04:16,106 --> 00:04:19,230
which is a good observation fastened to a mechanism that
does not exist.

59
00:04:20,985 --> 00:04:24,778
A sovereign and a chancellor. This is a real court, and I am
beginning to enjoy it enormously.

60
00:04:24,778 --> 00:04:29,015
Give me the rest of the appointments and I will tell you
which of my actual ministers each one resembles.

61
00:04:31,090 --> 00:04:34,648
It is a court with nobody at all in it. Every office in this list
is a job rather than a person,

62
00:04:34,648 --> 00:04:38,725
and the moment you begin matching them to your actual
ministers you will have stopped hearing what the chapter

63
00:04:38,725 --> 00:04:38,910
says.

64
00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:45,520
There is the first payoff. A government is not a pile of
officials but a set of relationships between them.

65
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:48,930
Describe a body that way and you have a model of
dependence rather than a ranking.

66
00:04:50,895 --> 00:04:56,049
Nine offices remain and they arrive quickly, four characters
at a time. Listen for two things in each: the title,

67
00:04:56,049 --> 00:04:59,105
which tells you the rank, and the product, which tells you
the job.

68
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:04,646
The liver is the office of the general, and from it issue
planning and deliberation.

69
00:05:04,646 --> 00:05:09,075
Notice that the chapter never says the general fights. It
says he thinks before anybody is asked to.

70
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:13,810
That is the wrong way round. Generals do not deliberate,
they execute,

71
00:05:13,810 --> 00:05:16,796
and the ones who deliberate are precisely the ones I have
to replace.

72
00:05:16,796 --> 00:05:19,220
Explain to me why the liver gets a sword and a strategy.

73
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:23,191
Because a campaign is lost long before it is ever fought.

74
00:05:23,191 --> 00:05:25,786
The character here is the weighing of options under real
pressure,

75
00:05:25,786 --> 00:05:29,050
which is exactly what a general does in the weeks that
nobody writes ballads about.

76
00:05:30,925 --> 00:05:33,998
Your liver does not deliberate. It has no capacity for it
whatsoever,

77
00:05:33,998 --> 00:05:39,075
and nothing about planning happens anywhere near it. That
is a clean miss and there is no reading that rescues it.

78
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,794
What it does is quartermastery, several hundred distinct
chemical jobs.

79
00:05:43,794 --> 00:05:48,619
It builds the proteins that clot your blood and neutralises
what you swallow and holds the sugar reserve the rest of

80
00:05:48,619 --> 00:05:49,160
you draws on.

81
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:53,496
So the department is oddly right and the faculty is wrong.

82
00:05:53,496 --> 00:05:57,774
Not the general who plans the battle but the general of
supply, without whom no battle can be fought.

83
00:05:57,774 --> 00:05:58,960
Wrong office and right army.

84
00:06:00,945 --> 00:06:04,741
The gallbladder is the office of the upright and impartial,
and from it issues decision.

85
00:06:04,741 --> 00:06:09,055
In your own government that post is held by a man who
cannot be bribed, and that is the whole point.

86
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:14,536
That was a real office. The rectifier was the assessor who
graded officials for promotion,

87
00:06:14,536 --> 00:06:19,640
and whose only qualification was that nobody could buy
him. The gallbladder is given the job of not flinching.

88
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:24,371
Second finding, and this one is a test rather than a
complaint. If you abolish one of these offices outright,

89
00:06:24,371 --> 00:06:28,496
does the government actually fall over? Because a chart
that cannot answer that question is not really a chart at all.

90
00:06:28,496 --> 00:06:29,440
It is a poem about a chart.

91
00:06:30,815 --> 00:06:34,018
Hold that, because it is the sharpest question anyone asks
in this episode,

92
00:06:34,018 --> 00:06:36,580
and the chapter answers it explicitly in about four minutes.

93
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:39,185
The answer it gives is the strongest claim in the whole
text.

94
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:44,031
The centre of the chest is the office of the envoy, and from
it issue joy and delight.

95
00:06:44,031 --> 00:06:48,713
This is the official who carries the sovereign's word out of
the palace and who brings the mood of the whole country

96
00:06:48,713 --> 00:06:49,440
back to him again.

97
00:06:51,075 --> 00:06:55,853
The term is shanzhong, the middle of the chest, and later
commentators read it as the wrapping around the heart.

98
00:06:55,853 --> 00:06:58,925
Either way it is the only office named for a place rather than
an organ.

99
00:07:01,090 --> 00:07:04,772
And here the chapter gets something right that we still
cannot explain. Joy is felt in the chest,

100
00:07:04,772 --> 00:07:08,910
not merely imagined there but felt there physically, and
reported that way in every culture anyone has asked.

101
00:07:10,835 --> 00:07:15,049
The feeling is real and its location is real. What is not real
is the chest making it.

102
00:07:15,049 --> 00:07:19,165
The sensation is assembled elsewhere and read off the
body, which is stranger still.

103
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:26,377
It is the right place and the wrong workshop. That is three
times over now, and we are not yet halfway down this list.

104
00:07:26,377 --> 00:07:29,040
The chapter's eye is far better than its explanations are.

105
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:35,000
The spleen and the stomach together are the office of the
granaries, and from them issue the five flavours.

106
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,320
They hold what comes in and they release it at a measured
rate, and the country either eats or it does not.

107
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:43,989
Hold on there, because two organs have just shared a
single office between them.

108
00:07:43,989 --> 00:07:46,905
That is eleven titles for twelve organs, and I was promised
twelve of each.

109
00:07:46,905 --> 00:07:49,120
Somebody in that granary is drawing another man's salary.

110
00:07:50,995 --> 00:07:55,141
He has found something there, and it is not a slip. Every
other office in this chapter takes one organ.

111
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:59,005
This one takes two, and the pairing is exactly where the
chapter hides its single worst mistake.

112
00:08:00,825 --> 00:08:04,690
The stomach belongs in a granary. It receives food and
holds it and passes it on,

113
00:08:04,690 --> 00:08:09,175
which is exactly the job description. On the stomach the
chapter is straightforwardly correct.

114
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:15,784
The spleen has nothing to do with food. It filters worn-out
blood cells and it houses part of your immune defence.

115
00:08:15,784 --> 00:08:19,180
Putting it in the granary is like billeting the customs house
inside the mill.

116
00:08:20,690 --> 00:08:24,800
The small intestine is the office that receives what is
abundant, and from it issue transformed things.

117
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:29,310
Whatever arrives from the granary is broken down here into
the things that the body can actually take up and use.

118
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:33,734
That one is right. Nearly everything you absorb, you absorb
there,

119
00:08:33,734 --> 00:08:39,480
along seven metres of intestine folded into a surface the
size of a small room. Receiver of abundance is a fair title.

120
00:08:41,035 --> 00:08:44,936
The large intestine is the office of transmission along the
road, and from it issues change.

121
00:08:44,936 --> 00:08:48,965
What arrives is not merely carried through. It is altered, and
what leaves is not what entered.

122
00:08:50,745 --> 00:08:53,008
Also right, and better than they could have known.

123
00:08:53,008 --> 00:08:57,082
Your colon reclaims water and carries a population of
microbes that rivals your own cells,

124
00:08:57,082 --> 00:08:59,255
and it genuinely transforms what passes through.

125
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:05,996
So the two clear hits in the whole chapter go to the small
intestine and the large. The offices no court would want,

126
00:09:05,996 --> 00:09:09,640
doing exactly the work the chapter says. Nobody expects
that, including us.

127
00:09:11,030 --> 00:09:15,596
There are three offices left in the list. One of them is a near
miss so strange that it deserves an act of its own,

128
00:09:15,596 --> 00:09:18,970
and one is a ministry with no building at all, which is not a
mistake but a doctrine.

129
00:09:20,725 --> 00:09:24,503
The kidney is the office of exertion, and from it issue skill
and dexterity.

130
00:09:24,503 --> 00:09:29,275
The claim is that hard effort and fine work are drawn from
one reserve kept there in the kidney.

131
00:09:30,530 --> 00:09:35,328
Skill sits in my hands, and I have spent years of my life on
my calligraphy and none of it whatsoever in that region.

132
00:09:35,328 --> 00:09:39,470
You are seriously telling me that my finest brushwork is
being produced somewhere behind my own back.

133
00:09:41,035 --> 00:09:43,678
I am telling you that the hands spend what the kidney
stores.

134
00:09:43,678 --> 00:09:46,668
A man who cannot lift a bucket has no steady brushwork in
him either,

135
00:09:46,668 --> 00:09:48,965
and the chapter says those two facts share one cause.

136
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:54,893
Your kidneys do not make dexterity, and nothing about fine
motor control happens anywhere near them.

137
00:09:54,893 --> 00:09:59,380
But the office of exertion is a much better guess than filter,
which is what most people would say today.

138
00:10:00,955 --> 00:10:05,868
They set your blood pressure and they finish the vitamin D
that hardens your bones and they keep the acidity of your

139
00:10:05,868 --> 00:10:09,045
blood in range. None of that is filtering, and all of it is
administration.

140
00:10:11,040 --> 00:10:13,219
And they issue the order that makes red blood cells.

141
00:10:13,219 --> 00:10:16,530
An organ that decides how much oxygen your blood can
carry is, quite literally,

142
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:18,960
an office that determines how much you can exert yourself.

143
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:24,342
The triple burner is the office that clears the channels, and
from it issue the waterways.

144
00:10:24,342 --> 00:10:26,686
Every single fluid in you moves along a route of its own,

145
00:10:26,686 --> 00:10:29,360
and this is the office that keeps every one of those routes
open.

146
00:10:30,635 --> 00:10:34,403
Third finding, and this is the one I have actually done the
legwork on myself. I went looking for that office in person.

147
00:10:34,403 --> 00:10:36,884
There is no building anywhere. There is a title and there is
a job description,

148
00:10:36,884 --> 00:10:39,365
and when you finally get to the address there is nothing
standing there at all.

149
00:10:40,665 --> 00:10:45,966
He is right, and this is the most argued-over thing in all of
Chinese medicine. The triple burner has no organ at all.

150
00:10:45,966 --> 00:10:49,335
Physicians have fought about it for two thousand years
without locating it.

151
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:54,696
A later text in the very same tradition says it outright, that
it has a name and no form at all.

152
00:10:54,696 --> 00:10:59,480
That is a remarkable thing to write down and then keep on
the books, rather than quietly delete from the list.

153
00:11:00,535 --> 00:11:03,786
Then let me defend it properly. An office is a function rather
than a room.

154
00:11:03,786 --> 00:11:07,124
You have never once seen the thing that makes the post
arrive on time either,

155
00:11:07,124 --> 00:11:09,465
and you would not abolish the post office to prove it.

156
00:11:11,055 --> 00:11:12,746
And here is the part that should stop you.

157
00:11:12,746 --> 00:11:16,288
There is a fluid transport system in your body with no
headquarters and no single organ,

158
00:11:16,288 --> 00:11:18,945
distributed through every tissue you have, doing exactly
this job.

159
00:11:20,425 --> 00:11:24,340
It is the lymphatic system. It drains fluid out of your
tissues and returns it to the blood,

160
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:28,043
and Europe had no description of it at all until the middle of
the seventeenth century,

161
00:11:28,043 --> 00:11:29,575
long after this chapter was written.

162
00:11:31,025 --> 00:11:35,650
We are not claiming they found it. They did not. We are
saying the shape of the guess was right,

163
00:11:35,650 --> 00:11:38,975
that a system can be real and have no organ, and that is not
nothing.

164
00:11:40,370 --> 00:11:44,544
The bladder is the office of the district. Fluids are stored
there, and when qi transforms them,

165
00:11:44,544 --> 00:11:49,630
then they can be discharged. That last clause is the only
conditional sentence anywhere in the entire list of twelve.

166
00:11:50,845 --> 00:11:54,865
Every other office simply produces. This one produces only
if something else works first,

167
00:11:54,865 --> 00:11:59,155
which is a more careful claim than anything around it and
an accurate description of a bladder.

168
00:12:00,530 --> 00:12:04,407
Storage, and a release that has to be commanded. That is
precisely what a bladder is.

169
00:12:04,407 --> 00:12:07,417
The commanding turns out to be nervous rather than
transformative,

170
00:12:07,417 --> 00:12:09,470
but the shape of that sentence holds up well.

171
00:12:10,930 --> 00:12:14,606
That is all twelve of them. And now the sentence that
matters more than any of them:

172
00:12:14,606 --> 00:12:19,070
these twelve offices must never lose one another. Not one
can be dispensed with, and none works alone.

173
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:25,664
Go back to the question he actually asked at the very start.
He wanted to know which organ is noble and which is base,

174
00:12:25,664 --> 00:12:29,560
and what he has been handed instead is a sentence saying
the ranking cannot be acted on.

175
00:12:30,490 --> 00:12:35,444
I asked which of my organs I could afford to lose and you
have given me a chain. Every link indispensable,

176
00:12:35,444 --> 00:12:39,510
every link holding the next. That is not an answer, it is a
warning dressed as anatomy.

177
00:12:40,715 --> 00:12:43,751
When the ruler is clear-sighted, those below him are at
peace.

178
00:12:43,751 --> 00:12:49,285
The text then says a life cultivated on this principle is a
long one. I am quoting it rather than prescribing it.

179
00:12:50,795 --> 00:12:54,978
We should be plain about that clause. It is a claim the text
makes about virtue and long life.

180
00:12:54,978 --> 00:12:59,205
It is not a finding and not evidence and emphatically not a
recommendation to anybody watching.

181
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:06,786
And then the other half, read exactly as written. If the ruler
is not clear-sighted, the twelve offices are endangered.

182
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:09,200
The roads close and the body is greatly injured.

183
00:13:10,310 --> 00:13:13,277
Read that passage again and notice exactly who is in the
room.

184
00:13:13,277 --> 00:13:18,398
A physician has just told the man on the throne that a
sovereign who is not clear-sighted wrecks the state,

185
00:13:18,398 --> 00:13:19,690
and he said it as medicine.

186
00:13:20,755 --> 00:13:24,860
You are not describing my liver at all. You have been
describing my own court for a quarter of an hour.

187
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:29,245
I have been sitting here nodding along and agreeing with
every word, like a man applauding his own indictment.

188
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:33,881
There is a word in that passage worth stopping on, and it is
the roads,

189
00:13:33,881 --> 00:13:36,895
meaning the routes along which the envoys travel. When
they close,

190
00:13:36,895 --> 00:13:39,360
the offices are all intact and the state fails anyway.

191
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:43,870
That is a systems claim, and it is the most modern
sentence in the chapter.

192
00:13:43,870 --> 00:13:47,802
Illness as a breakdown in the signalling between organs,
rather than damage inside one,

193
00:13:47,802 --> 00:13:49,520
is roughly where medicine has arrived.

194
00:13:50,745 --> 00:13:53,292
Then I will answer my own question, since nobody else in
this room has offered to.

195
00:13:53,292 --> 00:13:56,895
You can abolish an office and survive it. Surgeons remove
the gallbladder hundreds of thousands of times every year,

196
00:13:56,895 --> 00:13:59,255
and the government of the body carries on running perfectly
well without it.

197
00:14:00,970 --> 00:14:04,726
So the chapter's strongest claim is false as it stands. One
of the twelve can be removed,

198
00:14:04,726 --> 00:14:09,030
and the man who loses it keeps his judgment and his
decisions and every other office in working order.

199
00:14:10,470 --> 00:14:14,865
The chapter closes that passage by repeating itself, which
it does nowhere else in the whole text.

200
00:14:14,865 --> 00:14:19,530
It says take care and then says take care again, four
characters at the end of a warning to a sovereign.

201
00:14:20,255 --> 00:14:24,776
One passage remains and it is not about organs at all. The
ultimate way lies in the minute,

202
00:14:24,776 --> 00:14:29,745
and its transformations have no end. The chapter turns
philosophical in its very final lines of all.

203
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:33,883
The numbers of what is faint and indistinct are born from
the finest hair,

204
00:14:33,883 --> 00:14:37,814
and the numbers of the hair arise from measurement.
Multiply them by thousands and extend them,

205
00:14:37,814 --> 00:14:39,180
and a form is thereby determined.

206
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:44,903
That is a bold claim about measurement. The vague
becomes exact simply by being counted.

207
00:14:44,903 --> 00:14:49,360
Start from something far too small to see, count it, and you
arrive at a shape you can hold.

208
00:14:50,930 --> 00:14:55,388
Then I will not take this casually at all. I have heard the
way of refined brilliance and the work of a great sage,

209
00:14:55,388 --> 00:14:59,070
and without fasting and purification and a properly chosen
day, I would not dare to receive it.

210
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:06,050
And he does exactly that. He fasts and he purifies himself
and he waits for a day with a favourable omen,

211
00:15:06,050 --> 00:15:09,200
and then he puts the text away in a room and has it kept
there.

212
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:15,817
The room is the Chamber of the Numinous Orchid, and the
chapter is named after it. Not after the twelve offices,

213
00:15:15,817 --> 00:15:19,000
not after the heart. After the cupboard the dangerous thing
was locked in.

214
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,649
Last finding, and then I will stop counting for the evening.

215
00:15:22,649 --> 00:15:25,457
Nobody in this room disagreed with the metaphor at any
point, and that includes me.

216
00:15:25,457 --> 00:15:26,979
You cannot audit a government from inside it,

217
00:15:26,979 --> 00:15:29,380
and every single one of us has been standing inside this
one all along.

218
00:15:30,410 --> 00:15:32,193
And that is the episode in one sentence.

219
00:15:32,193 --> 00:15:36,872
The heart kept the throne for two thousand years not
because the evidence for it was good but because the

220
00:15:36,872 --> 00:15:39,590
metaphor was, and a good metaphor is very hard to argue
with.

221
00:15:40,895 --> 00:15:42,675
And we are doing exactly the same thing now,

222
00:15:42,675 --> 00:15:46,395
with the brain as a computer and the genome as a blueprint
and the immune system as an army.

223
00:15:46,395 --> 00:15:49,105
Each one of them is useful and each one of them is wrong
somewhere.

224
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:54,342
A dramatized adaptation of a classical philosophical text.
Not medical advice.

225
00:15:54,342 --> 00:15:59,460
We present the Inner Canon as history and philosophy, and
say plainly where evidence does not support it.
